# self-contained: the inbound message(s), the world state they land in,
# the surrounding chat history the Pi really forwards, the actor, and
# the KNOWN-CORRECT outcome expressed as writes and decisions.
#
# Ground truth comes from the commit named in each `provenance` block.
# Never add a case you cannot substantiate: if the redesign doc is the
# only source, say so with provenance.kind = "doc".
#
# Expectations assert the DATABASE and whether MatchTime speaks at all.
# Where copy matters they assert PROPERTIES (names a player, does not
# claim a move that did not happen, no raw phone number) — never a
# golden string, which would rot on the next copy tweak.
#
# A stubbed case says, per message, what the ROUTER answered (`route`)
