MatchTime","body":"🗓 *Tuesday 7-a-side* — Tue 21:30 at Goals North Cheam.\n\n*Confirmed (11/14):*\n1. Kemal Ediz\n2. Elvin Aliyev\n3. Sait Demir\n4. Mustafa Kaya\n5. Abid Hussain\n6. Idris Bello\n7. Faris Nasser\n8. Shaz Iqbal\n9. Adam Osman\n10. Efat Rahman\n11. Amir Ahmadi\n\nWe need *3 more*. Reply *IN* to grab a spot."}],"messages":[{"from":"zair","tag":true,"body":"@Match Time Amir paid for 4 players","route":"admin_ops","facts":{"action":"bulk_payment","payerRef":"Amir","count":4}}],"expect":{"unchanged":true,"speaks":"silent"},"tags":["payments","authorisation"],"stubKind":"transcribed","contractTagAdded":true,"notes":"FIDELITY CAVEAT: the production message was UNTAGGED. It carries an @Match Time tag here because the interaction contract (19f43e3, 2026-06-18, narrowed by bd3305d) landed AFTER this incident and now requires a tag for every directed op, so the untagged original can no longer reach the behaviour this case exists to pin. See the 2026-09-01 note in MDs/analyzer-redesign-2026-08-31.md section 3.2. NOT CANARIED, and this one cannot honestly be (2026-09-08). The assertion that would make it fail against a silent pipeline is 'no PaymentCredit row was created', and `CorpusObservation` carries attendance, members, speech, DMs, reacts, offers, teams and the score — no payment state. A canary write would also destroy `speaks: silent`, which IS the recorded outcome here. What the case does carry after the port is the dangerous direction: the facts ask for the credit, so it fails if authorisation ever stops refusing.","adjudication":{"verdict":"new_right","date":"2026-09-08","reason":"`speaks: silent` is added; `unchanged` stands. The provenance says a non-admin's credit is 'silently dropped', so silence is part of the known-correct outcome and was simply not asserted. The facts are byte-identical to S21's, so the only variable left is the sender's seat."}}
