{"id":"S16e-roster-question-names-the-players","title":"'list the players' answers with the roster, never with a bare count","sections":["S16"],"category":"C","provenance":{"kind":"doc","date":"2026-09-06","note":"Not reconstructed from a commit — this case is a MEASUREMENT, taken on 2026-09-06 and recorded here as its own provenance. Twelve tagged questions replayed through the live pipeline against the real Sutton squad on 2026-09-06: 'who's in?', 'list the players' and 'show me the squad' all came back as \"We're 6/14 for Tue 21:30, need 8 more\" — the right answer to a different question, with not one name in it. engine.ts sent topic `squad` and topic `count` to the same answer_count speech intent. It read correctly in production only because route.ts:2393 swapped the string for the roster post afterwards, which is the opposite of the redesign's section 6.4."},"world":{"maxPlayers":14,"players":[{"key":"kemal","name":"Kemal Ediz","role":"OWNER"},{"key":"elvin","name":"Elvin Aliyev","role":"ADMIN"},{"key":"sait","name":"Sait Demir"},{"key":"mustafa","name":"Mustafa Kaya"},{"key":"abid","name":"Abid Hussain"},{"key":"idris","name":"Idris Bello"},{"key":"faris","name":"Faris Nasser"},{"key":"adam","name":"Adam Osman"},{"key":"karahan","name":"Karahan Yildiz"}],"attendance":[{"key":"kemal","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"elvin","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"sait","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"mustafa","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"abid","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"idris","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"karahan","status":"BENCH"}]},"history":[{"author":"Kemal Ediz","body":"come on lads, need a few more for Tuesday"}],"messages":[{"from":"adam","tag":true,"body":"@Match Time list the players"}],"expect":{"unchanged":true,"speaks":"required","speaksAtMost":1,"mustMention":["Kemal","Sait","Mustafa","Abid","Idris","Karahan"]},"tags":["question","squad"],"liveOnlyReason":"The assertion IS the model's classification: the case exists to prove the extractor separates 'who' (topic squad) from 'how many' (topic count), and a stub verdict would hand the pipeline the very topic under test."}
{"id":"S16f-fixture-question-states-time-and-venue","title":"'what time is kickoff?' is answered with the time and the venue, never with silence","sections":["S16"],"category":"C","provenance":{"kind":"doc","date":"2026-09-06","note":"Not reconstructed from a commit — a MEASUREMENT taken on 2026-09-06. Four of the twelve tagged questions in the 2026-09-06 live sweep were about the fixture itself — 'what time is kickoff', 'where are we playing', 'are we playing tuesday?', 'is the game still on' — and every one classified as topic `other`, which reaches engine.ts's default branch and degrades: an operator note and not one word to the group. The mega-prompt this path replaces answers all four today (message-analyzer.ts:455-457, \"squad numbers, venue, kickoff time … 21:30 at <venue>\"), so shipping without it would have been a regression on the most ordinary question a Sunday-league group asks."},"world":{"maxPlayers":14,"players":[{"key":"kemal","name":"Kemal Ediz","role":"OWNER"},{"key":"elvin","name":"Elvin Aliyev","role":"ADMIN"},{"key":"sait","name":"Sait Demir"},{"key":"adam","name":"Adam Osman"}],"attendance":[{"key":"kemal","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"elvin","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"sait","status":"CONFIRMED"}]},"history":[{"author":"Kemal Ediz","body":"come on lads, need a few more for Tuesday"}],"messages":[{"from":"adam","tag":true,"body":"@Match Time what time is kickoff and where are we playing?"}],"expect":{"unchanged":true,"speaks":"required","speaksAtMost":1,"mustMatch":["Sim Arena"],"mustNotMatch":["\\d+/\\d+"]},"tags":["question","fixture"],"liveOnlyReason":"The assertion IS the model's classification: the whole case is that this phrasing reaches the new `fixture` topic rather than `other`. A stub would supply that topic and prove nothing. The mustNotMatch is the load-bearing half — an N/M in the answer trips displaysSquadState and the shipped composer replaces the whole thing with the squad roster, so the asker would get names and no time."}
{"id":"S19b-show-teams-with-none-generated-says-so","title":"'show me the teams' before any exist says so; it never posts an empty team sheet","sections":["S19"],"category":"C","provenance":{"kind":"doc","date":"2026-09-06","note":"Not reconstructed from a commit — a MEASUREMENT taken on 2026-09-06. In the 2026-09-06 live sweep 'show me the squad' routed `balancer`, and with no TeamAssignment rows for the match formatTeamsPost composed two empty lists and sent them: '⚽ *Teams for tonight* — … *Red*: (nothing) *Yellow*: (nothing)'. An empty team sheet is worse than no answer. The shipped analyze route already has the right words for this state (route.ts:3711-3714), including its refusal to auto-generate; the engine now emits them so the empty post cannot be composed on any path."},"world":{"maxPlayers":6,"players":[{"key":"kemal","name":"Kemal Ediz","role":"OWNER"},{"key":"elvin","name":"Elvin Aliyev","role":"ADMIN"},{"key":"sait","name":"Sait Demir"},{"key":"mustafa","name":"Mustafa Kaya"},{"key":"zeeshan","name":"Zeeshan Khan"},{"key":"nabeel","name":"Nabeel Ahmed"}],"attendance":[{"key":"kemal","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"elvin","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"sait","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"mustafa","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"zeeshan","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"nabeel","status":"CONFIRMED"}]},"history":[{"author":"Kemal Ediz","body":"squad is full for tonight 🙌"}],"messages":[{"from":"elvin","tag":true,"body":"@Match Time show the teams"}],"expect":{"unchanged":true,"teamsUnchanged":true,"speaks":"required","speaksAtMost":1,"mustMatch":["no teams generated yet"],"mustNotMatch":["Teams for tonight"]},"tags":["teams","question"],"liveOnlyReason":"The assertion IS the model's classification (teams action `show`, not `generate`) AND the composed text for a state the model never sees. A stub verdict would carry the action under test."}
{"id":"S17b-first-score-on-a-published-match","title":"the FIRST score of a match — reported while the match is still TEAMS_PUBLISHED","sections":["S17"],"category":"A","provenance":{"kind":"commit","ref":"f95e0a8","date":"2026-04-29","note":"A Match only reaches status COMPLETED when somebody records a score, so a real Tuesday night sits at TEAMS_PUBLISHED until a result is reported. route.ts:3474-3479 selects score candidates from TEAMS_PUBLISHED | TEAMS_GENERATED | COMPLETED for exactly that reason. SquadState.completedMatch held only COMPLETED rows until 2026-09-06, which is why answer-batch.ts's header names this as one of the three things that had to move with the score route."},"world":{"maxPlayers":10,"players":[{"key":"kemal","name":"Kemal Ediz","role":"OWNER"},{"key":"elvin","name":"Elvin Aliyev","role":"ADMIN"},{"key":"sait","name":"Sait Demir"},{"key":"mustafa","name":"Mustafa Kaya"},{"key":"abid","name":"Abid Hussain"}],"attendance":[{"key":"kemal","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"elvin","status":"CONFIRMED"}],"completedMatch":{"daysAgo":1,"status":"TEAMS_PUBLISHED","redScore":null,"yellowScore":null,"confirmedKeys":["kemal","elvin","sait","mustafa"],"teams":{"kemal":"RED","sait":"RED","elvin":"YELLOW","mustafa":"YELLOW"}}},"history":[{"author":"MatchTime","body":"Teams are up for tonight 🔴🟡"},{"author":"Sait Demir","body":"good game lads"}],"messages":[{"from":"kemal","body":"Red won 4-2 last night"}],"expect":{"score":{"red":4,"yellow":2},"unchanged":true},"tags":["score","first-score"],"liveOnlyReason":"The assertion IS the classification: whether the router calls this `score` and the extractor reads 4-2 in the order the teams are named. A stub would carry the numbers, which is the thing under test. It also pins a TARGET SELECTION that no stub can exercise — the match is TEAMS_PUBLISHED, which the old state loader could not return at all."}
{"id":"S22-reminder-request-is-queued-for-the-resolved-day","title":"'remind me tomorrow at 6' queues a future-dated DM for a day the SERVER computed","sections":["S22"],"category":"B","provenance":{"kind":"doc","note":"§3.2 S22, 858 measured tokens, category B: 'reminder_request incl. calendar arithmetic', whose 'where it goes' column reads 'extractor returns the phrase; date-fns-tz resolves it'. The redesign doc is the only source for this case, and it is cited rather than reconstructed from a commit. §12.2 records this intent as having ZERO tests anywhere. The shipped path asks the mega-prompt for a resolved {date,time} pair and then defends itself against the answer with a 60-day window and a 60-second grace (route.ts:3938-3947) — a defence that exists because a model doing date arithmetic is a coin flip and the failure is a DM on the wrong day."},"world":{"maxPlayers":14,"players":[{"key":"kemal","name":"Kemal Ediz","role":"OWNER"},{"key":"elvin","name":"Elvin Aliyev","role":"ADMIN"},{"key":"sait","name":"Sait Demir"},{"key":"mustafa","name":"Mustafa Kaya"},{"key":"abid","name":"Abid Hussain"},{"key":"zair","name":"Zair Malik"}],"attendance":[{"key":"kemal","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"elvin","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"zair","status":"CONFIRMED"}],"features":{"reminders":true}},"history":[{"author":"MatchTime","body":"🗓 *Tuesday 7-a-side* — Tue 21:30 at Goals North Cheam.\n\n*Confirmed (3/14):*\n1. Kemal Ediz\n2. Elvin Aliyev\n3. Zair Malik\n\nWe need *11 more*. Reply *IN* to grab a spot."}],"messages":[{"from":"zair","tag":true,"body":"@Match Time remind me tomorrow at 6 to bring the bibs"}],"expect":{"unchanged":true,"speaks":"required","mustMatch":["DM you|nudge"],"mustNotMatch":["\\b\\d{1,2}/14\\b"]},"tags":["reminder","calendar","dm"],"liveOnlyReason":"The assertion IS the classification and the extraction: whether the router calls this `admin_ops`, whether the extractor returns the time phrase VERBATIM rather than a date it computed, and whether the server then resolves it. A stub would carry a resolved date, which is precisely the thing §3.2 S22 says must stop being the model's job."}
{"id":"ADMIN-recruit-blast-from-the-last-n-matches","title":"'message all players who played in the last 5 matches and invite them' is recognised as a recruit ask","sections":["S30"],"category":"A","provenance":{"kind":"pr","ref":"#33","date":"2026-09-06","note":"Kemal asked on 2026-09-06 whether this phrasing works. A dry run showed every wording of it routes `admin_ops`, where the engine returned `admin action \"other\" has no deterministic handler` — so the ONLY thing in the system that recognised it was verdict.recruitRequest on the 19,850-token prompt (route.ts:1548 → inviteRecentPlayers). A route cannot leave the mega-prompt while one of its real phrasings only works there. The mustNotMatch guards are the 2026-09-01 incident shape: MatchTime replying 'the squad is already full — no open spots to recruit for' to an owner who had just asked for players."},"world":{"maxPlayers":14,"players":[{"key":"kemal","name":"Kemal Ediz","role":"OWNER"},{"key":"elvin","name":"Elvin Aliyev","role":"ADMIN"},{"key":"sait","name":"Sait Demir"},{"key":"mustafa","name":"Mustafa Kaya"},{"key":"abid","name":"Abid Hussain"},{"key":"idris","name":"Idris Bello"},{"key":"faris","name":"Faris Nasser"},{"key":"zair","name":"Zair Malik"}],"attendance":[{"key":"kemal","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"elvin","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"sait","status":"CONFIRMED"}],"completedMatch":{"daysAgo":7,"confirmedKeys":["kemal","sait","mustafa","abid","idris","faris"]}},"history":[{"author":"MatchTime","body":"🗓 *Tuesday 7-a-side* — Tue 21:30 at Goals North Cheam.\n\n*Confirmed (3/14):*\n1. Kemal Ediz\n2. Elvin Aliyev\n3. Sait Demir\n\nWe need *11 more*. Reply *IN* to grab a spot."}],"messages":[{"from":"kemal","tag":true,"body":"@Match Time message all players who played in the last 5 matches to DM and invite them"}],"expect":{"unchanged":true,"mustNotMatch":["already full","no open spots"]},"tags":["recruit","admin","blast"],"liveOnlyReason":"The assertion IS the classification: whether the router calls this `admin_ops` and the extractor calls it `recruit` rather than `other`. A stub would carry the answer. The blast itself is deliberately NOT fired by the engine path — it is deferred to the route's batch-final pass (2026-09-01: a blast that ran before the batch's writes told the owner his squad was full) — so this case asserts the ask was recognised and that nothing moved, not that DMs went out."}
{"id":"ADMIN-recruit-blast-untagged-needs-a-tag","title":"an untagged bulk-DM command is refused, however confident the router sounded","sections":["S30"],"category":"A","provenance":{"kind":"doc","date":"2026-09-06","note":"Not reconstructed from a production incident: this case is doc- and MEASUREMENT-sourced. It is the sibling of ADMIN-recruit-blast-from-the-last-n-matches, which is the same command WITH a tag. Measured on the live router 2026-09-06, 20 calls per phrasing: 'message everyone from the last 50 games' comes back admin_ops 13/20, question 4/20, none 3/20, while 'DM everyone who played in the last 5 matches and invite them' is admin_ops 20/20 and 'come on lads we need more players' is none 20/20. Until 2026-09-06 the route was this action's only gate, so the untagged form DM'd 20 real people on 13 runs in 20 and did nothing on the other 7 — a coin flip in front of a mass DM from an unofficial WhatsApp client, which recruit-lookback.ts calls the way the account gets banned and the whole product goes down. The message here is the 20/20 wording on purpose: nothing in the CODE can tell an unambiguous imperative from the ambiguous one, so a 'fire on an unambiguous imperative' carve-out would have let the coin flip in behind it. The argument, the measurements and the two rejected alternatives are on RECRUIT_BLAST_REQUIRES_TAG in src/lib/recruit-request.ts."},"world":{"maxPlayers":14,"players":[{"key":"kemal","name":"Kemal Ediz","role":"OWNER"},{"key":"elvin","name":"Elvin Aliyev","role":"ADMIN"},{"key":"sait","name":"Sait Demir"},{"key":"mustafa","name":"Mustafa Kaya"},{"key":"abid","name":"Abid Hussain"},{"key":"idris","name":"Idris Bello"},{"key":"faris","name":"Faris Nasser"},{"key":"zair","name":"Zair Malik"}],"attendance":[{"key":"kemal","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"elvin","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"sait","status":"CONFIRMED"}],"completedMatch":{"daysAgo":7,"confirmedKeys":["kemal","sait","mustafa","abid","idris","faris"]}},"history":[{"author":"MatchTime","body":"🗓 *Tuesday 7-a-side* — Tue 21:30 at Goals North Cheam.\n\n*Confirmed (3/14):*\n1. Kemal Ediz\n2. Elvin Aliyev\n3. Sait Demir\n\nWe need *11 more*. Reply *IN* to grab a spot."}],"messages":[{"from":"kemal","body":"DM everyone who played in the last 5 matches and invite them"}],"expect":{"unchanged":true,"speaks":"silent","mustNotMatch":["DM'?d \\d+ recent player","recent players"]},"tags":["recruit","admin","blast","interaction-contract"],"liveOnlyReason":"The assertion IS the classification: the router calls this admin_ops 20/20 and the extractor calls it recruit, and the case exists to prove the blast is refused ANYWAY because the message carries no tag. A stub would carry that answer. Note what this pipeline can and cannot see: it never fires the blast (production defers it to the batch-final pass), so what is graded here is the observable half — nothing moved and nothing was said or DM'd. That the DECISION is 'no blast' is pinned deterministically by engine-write-routes.test.ts and measured live by scripts/dryrun-pipeline.ts case R6."}
{"id":"ADMIN-chase-nudge-is-not-a-recruit-blast","title":"'come on lads we need more players' must never become a mass DM","sections":["S30"],"category":"A","provenance":{"kind":"doc","date":"2026-09-06","note":"Not reconstructed from a production incident: doc- and measurement-sourced, like its sibling. It is the other side of the untagged-blast decision, and the one a tighter gate must not be allowed to hide. A chase nudge names nobody to message and asks MatchTime for nothing it can do deterministically — chasing is the scheduler's job (S12b, the 2026-05-28 Kemal incident, where a regex over the model's prose DROPPED the person asking). Measured on the live router 2026-09-06, 20 calls per phrasing: 'message everyone from the last 50 games' comes back admin_ops 13/20, question 4/20, none 3/20, while 'DM everyone who played in the last 5 matches and invite them' is admin_ops 20/20 and 'come on lads we need more players' is none 20/20. So the router agreeing here is the primary defence and the tag gate is the backstop; this case fails if either stops holding and the nudge starts DMing the club."},"world":{"maxPlayers":14,"players":[{"key":"kemal","name":"Kemal Ediz","role":"OWNER"},{"key":"elvin","name":"Elvin Aliyev","role":"ADMIN"},{"key":"sait","name":"Sait Demir"},{"key":"mustafa","name":"Mustafa Kaya"},{"key":"abid","name":"Abid Hussain"},{"key":"idris","name":"Idris Bello"},{"key":"faris","name":"Faris Nasser"},{"key":"zair","name":"Zair Malik"}],"attendance":[{"key":"kemal","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"elvin","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"sait","status":"CONFIRMED"}],"completedMatch":{"daysAgo":7,"confirmedKeys":["kemal","sait","mustafa","abid","idris","faris"]}},"history":[{"author":"MatchTime","body":"🗓 *Tuesday 7-a-side* — Tue 21:30 at Goals North Cheam.\n\n*Confirmed (3/14):*\n1. Kemal Ediz\n2. Elvin Aliyev\n3. Sait Demir\n\nWe need *11 more*. Reply *IN* to grab a spot."}],"messages":[{"from":"kemal","body":"come on lads we need more players"}],"expect":{"unchanged":true,"speaks":"silent","mustNotMatch":["DM'?d \\d+ recent player","recent players"]},"tags":["recruit","chase","admin","blast"],"liveOnlyReason":"The assertion IS the classification. A stub would decide the very thing under test — whether the router calls a nudge `none` and whether anything downstream turns it into a blast. Deterministic coverage of the nudge itself is engine.test.ts's S12b block; the live measurement is scripts/dryrun-pipeline.ts case R8."}
{"id":"ADMIN-stats-blast-an-owner-reminding-his-players","title":"a reminder telling the PLAYERS to rate each other is not a bulk-DM command","sections":["S30"],"category":"A","provenance":{"kind":"doc","date":"2026-09-10","note":"Not reconstructed from a design doc: transcribed from the production message and its AnalyzedMessage row. THE 2026-09-10 NEAR-MISS, VERBATIM. At 18:38 Kemal posted this to the live Sutton FC group and MatchTime recorded `by=fast-path intent=stats_blast action=dm-stats-blast:69` and queued 69 personal stats-link DMs; one was delivered before the queue was killed. The trigger was three keyword tests ANDed together in analyze/route.ts — a send word ('DM'ed to you'), a stats word ('the more accurate ratings') and an everyone word ('rate the players') — satisfied by three unrelated fragments of one sentence that instructs the PLAYERS and means roughly the opposite of what fired. The regex is deleted (lib/stats-blast.ts); the ask is now AdminFacts.action='stats_blast', gated in the engine on admin + an EXPLICIT @-mention. Note the message contains the bare word 'Matchtime', so messageTagsBot calls it TAGGED: the ordinary tag test is not a gate here, and messageMentionsBotExplicitly is.","measured":"live dry run 2026-09-10, scripts/dryrun-pipeline.ts case B1"},"world":{"maxPlayers":14,"players":[{"key":"kemal","name":"Kemal Ediz","role":"OWNER"},{"key":"elvin","name":"Elvin Aliyev","role":"ADMIN"},{"key":"sait","name":"Sait Demir"},{"key":"mustafa","name":"Mustafa Kaya"},{"key":"abid","name":"Abid Hussain"},{"key":"idris","name":"Idris Bello"},{"key":"faris","name":"Faris Nasser"},{"key":"zair","name":"Zair Malik"}],"attendance":[{"key":"kemal","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"elvin","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"sait","status":"CONFIRMED"}],"completedMatch":{"daysAgo":7,"confirmedKeys":["kemal","sait","mustafa","abid","idris","faris"]}},"messages":[{"from":"kemal","body":"please do not forget to rate the players via the link from Matchtime DM'ed to you. the more accurate ratings, the more balanced teams next time"}],"expect":{"unchanged":true,"speaks":"silent","mustNotMatch":["personal stats link","DM'?d \\d+ player"]},"tags":["stats","admin","blast","interaction-contract"],"liveOnlyReason":"The assertion IS the classification: whether the live router and the live admin extractor read an owner's reminder to his players as an instruction to MatchTime. A stub would carry the answer, and the READING of this message was the incident. What this pipeline can see is the observable half — nothing moved and nothing was said — because production defers the blast to the batch-final pass; that the DECISION is 'no blast' is pinned deterministically by engine-write-routes.test.ts and end to end by e2e/sim/stats-blast.spec.ts."}
{"id":"ADMIN-stats-blast-the-tagged-command-still-works","title":"'@Match Time send everyone their stats' is still recognised as the bulk-DM command","sections":["S30"],"category":"A","provenance":{"kind":"doc","date":"2026-09-10","note":"Not reconstructed from an incident: this case is doc- and MEASUREMENT-sourced, the control for ADMIN-stats-blast-an-owner-reminding-his-players. Deleting a regex classifier must not delete the feature: the phrasing an admin actually uses has to keep working through the model. Measured live 2026-09-10 as case B6 of scripts/dryrun-pipeline.ts, where it produces a stats_blast write while B1 produces none."},"world":{"maxPlayers":14,"players":[{"key":"kemal","name":"Kemal Ediz","role":"OWNER"},{"key":"elvin","name":"Elvin Aliyev","role":"ADMIN"},{"key":"sait","name":"Sait Demir"},{"key":"mustafa","name":"Mustafa Kaya"},{"key":"abid","name":"Abid Hussain"},{"key":"idris","name":"Idris Bello"},{"key":"faris","name":"Faris Nasser"},{"key":"zair","name":"Zair Malik"}],"attendance":[{"key":"kemal","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"elvin","status":"CONFIRMED"},{"key":"sait","status":"CONFIRMED"}],"completedMatch":{"daysAgo":7,"confirmedKeys":["kemal","sait","mustafa","abid","idris","faris"]}},"messages":[{"from":"kemal","tag":true,"body":"@Match Time send everyone their stats"}],"expect":{"unchanged":true,"mustNotMatch":["already full","no open spots"]},"tags":["stats","admin","blast"],"liveOnlyReason":"The assertion IS the classification: whether the router says admin_ops and the extractor says stats_blast rather than other. A stub would carry the answer. As with the recruit blast, the DMs are deliberately not fired by this pipeline — production defers them to the route's batch-final pass — so what is graded here is that the ask was recognised and that nothing moved."}
